{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116310",
      "title": "Sending a GET Request To Fetch Data",
      "lectureOrder": 224,
      "videoOrder": 213,
      "sourceHash": "4b17a61590b30457e4463ffc2f10a8632ce5e00e4a1c95994a62c11864108d79",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.39,
          "en": "So let's use the injected HttpClient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.39,
          "end": 5.58,
          "en": "to fetch some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.58,
          "end": 9.06,
          "en": "And the question is, where do we put that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.06,
          "end": 11.46,
          "en": "for fetching that data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.46,
          "end": 14.58,
          "en": "And the answer is ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.58,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "would be a good place for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 21.75,
          "en": "Because here I want to fetch that places data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.75,
          "end": 24.45,
          "en": "from the backend right at the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.45,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "when this component becomes available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 31.17,
          "en": "so that I can populate the available places here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 32.343,
          "en": "right from the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.96,
          "end": 37.08,
          "en": "And therefore ngOnInit sounds like a great place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 40.23,
          "en": "to initialize this data fetching process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.23,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "because this method, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 44.673,
          "en": "will execute once the component is ready.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.08,
          "end": 48.7,
          "en": "Therefore I'll implement OnInit here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 54.48,
          "en": "and make sure to import that from @angular/core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 57.783,
          "en": "to rule out typos in the ngOnInit method name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.68,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "And then there we can use that HttpClient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 65.82300000000001,
          "en": "which we injected, and call one of the built-in methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.9,
          "end": 68.67,
          "en": "And as you can see, there are a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.67,
          "end": 71.73,
          "en": "of methods you can call on that HttpClient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.73,
          "end": 74.7,
          "en": "and in the end they represent different kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.7,
          "end": 79.7,
          "en": "of HTTP methods you could use for that outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 83.73,
          "en": "And if you wanna send a post request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 85.503,
          "en": "you would use the post method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 87.67,
          "en": "Now here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "I want to send a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 95.43,
          "en": "to the backend domain /places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.43,
          "end": 98.37299999999999,
          "en": "therefore it's the get method we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.17,
          "end": 102.53999999999999,
          "en": "And then get takes the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.53999999999999,
          "end": 104.523,
          "en": "to which you wanna send that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.45,
          "end": 110.45,
          "en": "For example, http://localhost:3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 114.39,
          "en": "which is the domain of that dummy backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.39,
          "end": 115.983,
          "en": "I provided to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 119.85,
          "en": "By default it's running on port 3000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 121.923,
          "en": "And then /places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.72,
          "end": 127.863,
          "en": "And this would send a get request to this URL here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.82,
          "end": 133.47,
          "en": "Now get then actually returns an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.47,
          "end": 135.54,
          "en": "and you learned about observables before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.54,
          "end": 139.26,
          "en": "So in the end it's a stream of data to which you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 140.47,
          "en": "and should subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.54,
          "end": 144.93,
          "en": "and you need to subscribe in order to really trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 148.38,
          "en": "that request because as you also learned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.38,
          "end": 150.9,
          "en": "if you just create an observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.9,
          "end": 154.17000000000002,
          "en": "which is what would happen if you don't call subscribe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.17000000000002,
          "end": 155.493,
          "en": "nothing would happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.39,
          "end": 160.113,
          "en": "So you want to subscribe here to trigger that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.94,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "And subscribe then takes such an observer object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 168.6,
          "en": "where you can define different functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.6,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "for different scenarios.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 173.07,
          "en": "For example, the next function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.07,
          "end": 175.473,
          "en": "to handle the next emitted value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.85,
          "end": 180.12,
          "en": "Now what's important to note about these observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 182.58,
          "en": "produced by HttpClient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 187.58,
          "en": "is that they'll only emit one value, typically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.01,
          "end": 189.27,
          "en": "I'm saying \"typically\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 192.27,
          "en": "because you could configure them in different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.27,
          "end": 196.29,
          "en": "and for example make sure that they emit more values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.29,
          "end": 201.29,
          "en": "But by default you would only get one value emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.36,
          "end": 204.32999999999998,
          "en": "and that would be the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.32999999999998,
          "end": 207.42000000000002,
          "en": "or to be precise, the response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.42000000000002,
          "end": 209.493,
          "en": "that's returned by the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 213.93,
          "en": "So here we can register a function which will get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.93,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "the response data and which can then use that response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 222.333,
          "en": "And for a start, I'll simply log it to the console here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.14,
          "end": 230.67000000000002,
          "en": "Now since those HttpClient methods typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.67000000000002,
          "end": 233.4,
          "en": "only produce one value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 238.4,
          "en": "you also don't necessarily need to unsubscribe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.5,
          "end": 242.76,
          "en": "but it's still considered a good practice to do so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.76,
          "end": 246.7,
          "en": "Therefore I will actually inject the destroyRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.97,
          "end": 250.533,
          "en": "hook here in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 253.353,
          "en": "like we did it before in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.55,
          "end": 257.253,
          "en": "and call this.destroyRef.onDestroy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.51,
          "end": 262.59,
          "en": "and make sure to clean up my HTTP subscription here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.59,
          "end": 264.63,
          "en": "So here I got the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 264.63,
          "end": 267.06,
          "en": "and in this onDestroy callback,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 267.06,
          "end": 269.193,
          "en": "I'll call unsubscribe on that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 270.66,
          "end": 274.08,
          "en": "Again, this is technically not necessarily required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.08,
          "end": 275.403,
          "en": "but it is a good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.02,
          "end": 278.64,
          "en": "What's also a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 278.64,
          "end": 282.75,
          "en": "is to give TypeScript some extra information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 282.75,
          "end": 286.203,
          "en": "about the kind of data we're getting back from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 287.25,
          "end": 289.59000000000003,
          "en": "At the moment, if you hover over resData here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 289.59000000000003,
          "end": 293.1,
          "en": "you see that it's just some kind of object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 293.1,
          "end": 296.58299999999997,
          "en": "So it could be any kind of data in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 297.65999999999997,
          "end": 300.903,
          "en": "And it is a good idea to be more specific here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 302.1,
          "end": 306.69,
          "en": "That's why you can add angle brackets after get or post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 306.69,
          "end": 308.55,
          "en": "or whatever you're using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 308.55,
          "end": 312.66,
          "en": "Here we need get, and between those angle brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 312.66,
          "end": 315.36,
          "en": "you can define the shape of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 315.36,
          "end": 318.57,
          "en": "that will be received in this next function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 318.57,
          "end": 322.68,
          "en": "So the shape of this response data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 325.59,
          "en": "And in my case here, that will be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 325.59,
          "end": 328.923,
          "en": "where we will have a places key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 329.94,
          "end": 332.37,
          "en": "And I know that we'll have such a places key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 332.37,
          "end": 337.353,
          "en": "because in the backend code I have that places key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 338.22,
          "end": 341.22,
          "en": "So that's the data that will be sent back from the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 341.22,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "and that is its shape, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 346.77,
          "en": "and it's an object with a places key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 346.77,
          "end": 349.98,
          "en": "And that places key will in the end hold an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 349.98,
          "end": 352.26,
          "en": "of place objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 352.26,
          "end": 355.23,
          "en": "where every object has such a shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 355.23,
          "end": 356.85,
          "en": "And conveniently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 356.85,
          "end": 361.17,
          "en": "that is the shape I defined here in my Angular app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 361.17,
          "end": 362.913,
          "en": "in the place model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 365.73,
          "end": 368.94,
          "en": "Therefore, in the available places component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 368.94,
          "end": 371.61,
          "en": "the type of data we'll get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 371.61,
          "end": 373.62,
          "en": "is an object with a places key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 373.62,
          "end": 376.71,
          "en": "where the value stored in that places key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 376.71,
          "end": 379.66,
          "en": "will be an array of places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 380.94,
          "end": 383.76,
          "en": "using that Place model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.76,
          "end": 386.13,
          "en": "So importing that Place model here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 386.13,
          "end": 390.213,
          "en": "and then using that here as an array, as a type of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 392.76,
          "end": 395.4,
          "en": "And that's some extra annotation we should add here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 395.4,
          "end": 397.95,
          "en": "so that we get better TypeScript support here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 397.95,
          "end": 401.37,
          "en": "in the place where we're trying to use that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 401.37,
          "end": 403.95,
          "en": "For example, I can now output the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 403.95,
          "end": 406.053,
          "en": "that are part of my response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 408.27,
          "end": 410.58,
          "en": "Well, and with that, if I save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 410.58,
          "end": 413.82,
          "en": "and I reload, you'll see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 413.82,
          "end": 417,
          "en": "after a while you'll see a response here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 417,
          "end": 418.953,
          "en": "you'll see those places here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 420.03,
          "end": 423.42,
          "en": "And it simply takes a while to fetch that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 423.42,
          "end": 428.11,
          "en": "because I deliberately added a delay here on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 429.15,
          "end": 433.02,
          "en": "because that will then later help us show some loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 433.02,
          "end": 436.323,
          "en": "to the user whilst we're waiting for the data to arrive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 437.82,
          "end": 440.61,
          "en": "So that's of course just some delay I added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 440.61,
          "end": 441.81,
          "en": "for demo purposes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 441.81,
          "end": 443.82,
          "en": "but it would be reasonable to assume",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 443.82,
          "end": 447.18,
          "en": "that your backend API might maybe at least sometimes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 447.18,
          "end": 448.56,
          "en": "be a bit slower,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 448.56,
          "end": 451.56,
          "en": "and you might wanna show some fallback content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 451.56,
          "end": 455.22,
          "en": "to the user whilst you're waiting for the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
